The framework (settled, do not relitigate)
Core claim: Perturbation is a property of the transformation, not the variable. Transformation is perturbation. The CNN's error is in the summarization, not the data.

ΔX(VAR) = the change in an analytic variable induced solely by transformation and allocation choices, holding the data source constant. VAR₀ = baseline at starting point A; VAR₁ = post-transformation value.

Agnostic to the analytic variable and to the baseline. The baseline need not be a direct observation — in this study it is not (it is the cropped, resized, quantized image). The framework measures change from wherever the study starts; it does not certify the start is unmediated.

Zero delta means the variable survived unchanged; it does not mean no perturbation occurred, and it does not mean the proxy is faithful. The allocation decision remains.

Not causal, not adjudicative. ΔX(VAR) records perturbation with magnitude and direction; it does not say which representation is correct, and does not treat zero delta as desirable.

The chain formula (settled as Form B):

E_total ≈ Σᵢ π(Tᵢ) · A(kᵢ) · Πⱼ>ᵢ Tⱼ

π(Tᵢ) = the true perturbation transformation *i* introduces. Property of the transformation, not the variable. This is what A(kᵢ) amplifies.

ΔX(VAR)ᵢ = the empirical measurement of π(Tᵢ) where measurement is possible. Not in the formula directly — it stands in for π(Tᵢ).

A(kᵢ) = amplification factor from observer state. kᵢ = known → A ≤ 1 (mitigation possible); kᵢ = unknown → A = ∞ (unbounded).

Πⱼ>ᵢ Tⱼ = cumulative downstream effect.

Critical: unknown links (where ΔX(VAR)ᵢ cannot be measured) are the ones where A = ∞. The ledger records them; it does not omit them. Unmeasured links are the most consequential, not the least.

Pickle clause: Knowing ΔX(VAR)ᵢ does not make π(Tᵢ) = 0; it makes A(kᵢ) finite. The perturbation remains; the amplification is bounded.

The shell game: The conflation of proxy with direct observation, made in ignorance that the proxy is a proxy, is what amplifies the perturbation. Biomedical research runs on proxies (organoids, organs-on-chips) and works because researchers know they are proxies. ML has not had this reckoning. Framing: first two noble truths — suffering exists (perturbation), suffering has an origin (ignorance of the allocation). The formula is diagnostic, not predictive; naming the terms is the intervention. "The analysis is different when you know. This study is an attempt to know."

The instrument (settled)
Restricted Boltzmann Machine — Gaussian-visible, chosen because it is generative: it reconstructs the input from its hidden representation. Reconstruction is the measurement.

No probes. A linear probe is a second model trained on the first model's output; it perturbs the thing it measures. Reconstruction is a forward pass through the model's own weights. This is a design commitment, not convenience.

Reconstruction ≠ distance. The residual (v_input − v_recon) measures the model's fidelity to its input — "does the character that went in look like the character coming out." It does not measure the distance from direct observation to proxy; that is named in the transformation ledger, not measured.

Lineage: Huffman coding (one object encodes/decodes; decode returns exact original) → RBM (decode returns a distribution; the difference is what we study). Han et al. (2015) merged CNN + Huffman for speed/energy; this is for information retention.

He et al. ResNet citation is used to argue that F(x) + x assumes operations are input-agnostic; Study 1 / Study 2 sign flips are evidence to the contrary.

