Key technical constraints for the code phase
No probes. Every measurement is reconstruction or a forward pass through the model's own weights. No fitted readout on hidden code. This is non-negotiable — it is the whole methodological point.

Reconstructions labeled by type: noise-off (one pass back through weights), median of draws (primary view), sampled (one draw). Median of draws is the primary view.

Preprocessing (2b): primary 32×32 (1,024 visible), 48×48 pilot arm if fine strokes lost. Ink dark and ink bright both in pilot. Primary scaling: per-pixel median removed, ÷ global MAD; comparison: mean/global SD (Hinton 2010). Scaling fitted on training folds only. No augmentation.

Training settings (2d): CD-1; lr 1e-3; momentum 0.5 (5 epochs) then 0.9; L2 1e-4 weights only; init N(0, 0.01); biases 0; mini-batch 10; epochs up to 300, stop when held-out free-energy gap widens.

Models (2c): GB (stochastic binary, biases yes), GR (noisy rectified max(0, x + N(0, σ(x))), biases yes), GR0 (noisy rectified, no hidden biases — the condition under which relative intensities are preserved per Nair & Hinton), GL optional (leaky, no published training recipe).

Outputs (2g): O1 filter atlas (full + top-36 by norm + random 36), O2 activity profile, O3 residual maps (signed, per-image; median absolute per character), O4 hidden-code geometry (within-model only — separately trained RBMs have unrelated units), O5 cross-source reconstruction, O6 gate decomposition, O7 stability/fit, O8 rebuilt images.

Free energy and reconstruction error mark when a model starts copying training images; they are not used to rank models. No likelihood measure.

Analysis plan (D): descriptive only; medians, IQR, full range, no means (except where distribution demonstrably symmetric); stratified bootstrap over seeds within folds (Agarwal et al. 2021, median for IQR mean); no unbiased K-fold variance estimator (Bengio & Grandvalet 2004), so fold intervals descriptive; every run reported, no best run; every summary number beside its picture.

